WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.680
Annihilation is a new sci-fi movie based on
a book by Jeff VanderMeer. It’s about an

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.990
alien place that grows and mutates and about
the people who it changes. It explores themes

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:17.840
of life and death, raises some cool mysteries,
and builds on the ideas of the book. The story

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.680
follows an expedition into the mysterious
Area X – a wilderness surrounded by a strange

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:29.110
“border” called the Shimmer . Anyone who
enters doesn’t return and the border is

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:34.070
growing . The team in the movie includes the
biologist Lena, the psychologist Ventress,

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.670
and the scientists Josie, Cass and Anya.
Together they enter the Area, and they find

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:45.499
mutant lifeforms like these colourful growths,
and strange hybrid creatures, like a plant

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:51.500
with different species of flower, an alligator
with teeth like a shark , and a man with slithering

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:57.889
snake-like guts. There are plants growing
in human shapes, and a mutant bear creature

00:00:57.889 --> 00:01:04.210
that speaks with Cass’ voice after it kills
her. So the Area makes new lifeforms by merging

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.980
existing ones together.
But there’s also duplication, making copies

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:13.620
of things – there’s a mutant deer that
mimics another deer’s movement. There’s

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.820
a double of Lena, which copies her movement
and her face. And we learn that Lena’s husband

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:24.820
Kane who returned from Area X is actually
an alien copy of the real Kane, who committed

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.240
suicide. The Area duplicates other stuff too.
Like, by the end of the movie, Lena gets a

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.010
tattoo that she didn’t have at the beginning.
It starts out as a bruise, but develops into

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:42.250
this ouroboros design – a copy of the same
tattoo on Anya and on this dead guy. The ouroboros

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:47.950
symbolises a cycle of life and death. There’s
also a house in Area X that looks just like

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:53.750
Lena’s place back home. So the Area doesn’t
just duplicate animals, it duplicates images,

00:01:53.750 --> 00:02:00.330
and even places based on memories.
The Area affects light and radio and magnetism,

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:06.220
it affects the team’s minds , it even affects
time – the team loses a few days at the

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.320
start . So the Area distorts, duplicates,
merges, mutates, and creates in a process

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:18.260
Josie calls refraction . And it all seems
to come from some alien presence in this lighthouse

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.370
. The movie shows that it’s extraterrestrial
– there’re shots of a meteor coming from

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:28.740
space and hitting the lighthouse. We don’t
know what the alien wants, or if it wants

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:34.260
at all – the movie suggests it’s like
a cancer, unthinking cells that just grow

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.650
and spread .
So while the alien in this movie represents

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:45.320
growth, the humans represent self-destruction.
Ventress says “almost all of us self-destruct”,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:51.190
it’s “coded into us” . Each character
hurts themselves somehow – Josie cuts herself

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.680
. Anya is “an addict” . Ventress has cancer
, and enters the Area as a sort of suicide.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.440
Lena has an affair with her douchey work colleague
who she hates , which hurts her relationship

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:07.270
with her husband Kane who she loves. And Kane
knows about Lena’s affair, which might be

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:13.459
partly why he volunteered for a dangerous
mission to Area X. Even this tattoo represents

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:19.760
self-destruction – it’s a snake eating
itself – destroying itself. So the humans

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.360
in this movie self-destruct – and this is
actually how they beat the alien in the end.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.940
Lena gives a grenade to the alien double that’s
mimicking her – she teaches it to blow itself

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.480
up. And the alien learns this self-destruction,
because that’s is its function – to duplicate

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:44.390
and assimilate. It assimilates its own annihilation.
So – the double burns, and takes the lighthouse

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:50.311
and Shimmer down with it. Humanity beats the
alien not through heroics or strength, but

00:03:50.311 --> 00:03:56.170
through our own flaws and weakness.
At the end of the movie, Lena reunites with

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:02.239
Kane, who she now knows is actually an alien
clone. And the Kane asks whether she is really

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:08.310
Lena . The movie ends with Lena’s eyes glowing
bright, which implies some kinda alien juju.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:14.280
So maybe this Lena is actually an alien clone.
Maybe the Shimmer didn’t really fall, it

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:20.350
just expanded to include the whole world.
The ending is deliberately ambiguous, but

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:26.280
this Lena probably is the real Lena. Cause
we saw the mimic Lena burn, and the real Lena

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:31.480
had been infected with glowing mutation from
early on – the glow’s nothing new. So

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:37.950
the ending might not mean that Lena is an
alien, it means that human Lena has changed.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:43.780
She taught the alien how to self-destruct
– maybe the alien taught her to grow.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.690
So the movie’s an exploration of life and
death, growth and change. The book explores

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:55.390
similar ideas, but the story’s quite different.
Like, Area X in the book doesn’t create

00:04:55.390 --> 00:05:01.370
much new mutant life – it’s more about
assimilation. People who enter the Area are

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:06.110
transformed to become part of the natural
environment – so there’s a dolphin with

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:11.660
a human eye , and a fox made of human cells,
as well as these creepy plant people . The

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:17.271
Area absorbs everything into itself , and
it spreads, by expanding its border, and by

00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:23.479
sending out clones to replace humans . The
mimicry and doubling is maybe like a “camouflage”

00:05:23.479 --> 00:05:28.770
used to hide its slow growth to replace everything
with an alien copy .

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:34.820
And the book hints at a kind of intelligence
behind this. Like, in the movie, the lighthouse

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:40.710
has a spooky H. R. Giger alien basement, but
the book has a whole tunnel structure separate

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:46.440
to the lighthouse. It’s like an alien upside-down
copy of the lighthouse. And it has a long

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:53.320
spiral staircase descending down, with a fungus
forming words on the walls. It reads “Where

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:58.020
lies the strangling fruit that came from the
hand of the sinner I shall bring forth the

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.770
seeds of the dead” and it goes on and on
like that. It’s as though the alien is trying

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:09.540
to absorb human ideas as well as human bodies.
The spiralling shape of the words looks kinda

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:15.740
like DNA. And the border is like a cell wall,
a membrane. So the whole Area seems kinda

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.910
like a biological cell. Which lends itself
to the cancer metaphor – a tumour growing

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:26.219
on the world.
In the book, none of the characters have names

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:31.340
– they’re just called the biologist, the
psychologist, anthropologist and surveyor.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:37.449
Their relationships are more cold, and suspicious.
The psychologist uses hypnotism to control

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:42.669
the others – makes them forget things, and
limits what they see . The government agency,

00:06:42.669 --> 00:06:48.350
the Southern Reach, is super mysterious and
manipulative. They lie to the group , withhold

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:52.230
information – it’s almost like they’re
experimenting on the expedition members as

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:58.539
much as on the Area . And the protagonist,
the biologist, is a complicated, highly introverted

00:06:58.539 --> 00:07:04.220
character – she’s sometimes an unreliable
narrator who misleads the reader . So the

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:10.661
book is super psychological, tense and paranoid.
But it’s also about the environment. For

00:07:10.661 --> 00:07:17.050
all the drama and mystery, the story is also
a love letter to the beauty and the strangeness

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.281
of nature.
